  "Help": "帮助",
  "# Amortization Tracker\n\nThis dashboard aims to show the depreciation value of the car over time and its journey.\n\nDepreciating a car by its mileage can be done using various methods. A common approach is to use a depreciation rate per mile or to create a depreciation curve based on data. On the other hand, the depreciation of a car due to age can vary depending on several factors such as the make, model, overall condition of the vehicle, and demand in the market.\n\nGenerally, it is estimated that a new car loses approximately 15% to 20% of its value in the first year. From there, the rate of depreciation tends to gradually decrease. Below is a rough estimate of the annual depreciation in the first few years:\n\n- First year: Around 15% to 20%.\n- Second year: Around 10% to 15%.\n- Third year and beyond: Around 5% to 10% annually.\n\nIt is important to remember that these values are approximate and may vary depending on individual circumstances. Also, some car models may hold their value better than others.\n\nAdditionally, some studies and experts suggest that a car loses a certain amount of value per mile driven. For instance, here we are using a standard rate 0.20 (use your currency) per mile or kilometer (depending on your preferred length unit)\n\n## Considerations for values in text boxes\n\nIn this panel we have both estimations: **Depreciation per Mileage** and **Depreciation per Age**\n\nSo fist of all you have to select:\n\n- Period to estimate (yearly or monthly)\n- Cost of your car\n- Depreciation percent % (of the first year). 20% by default as explained before\n- Loss rate per mile of kilometer. 0.2 (your currency) by default as explained before\n- Fuel price per mile of kilometer of your previous car (or a generic on equivalent to your actual Tesla)\n  \n  To calculate the cost per miles/kilometer of your car, you first need to determine how much it consumes in liters per 100 miles/kilometers. Then you can divide Consumption by mileage.\n\n  For example: let's say a car consumes 6 liters per 100km and the fuel costs 1.8€ per liter, we can calculate the actual consumption: 6/100 = 0.06 L/km\n  \n  Now, to determine the cost per kilometer, we multiply the actual consumption by the price of a liter of fuel (use your currency). For example 0.06L/km × 1.8€/L =0.108€/km (use miles or kms).\n  \n  Therefore, the cost per kilometer for your car would be approximately 0.108€. That's the value expected on the Fuel price textbox.\n\n## Data shown in the table\n\n- **Period**: Could be 'month' or 'year' depending what you've selected in the drop down list. So if selected as 'month', its going to be the data accumulated from 1st month at which TeslaMate started logging data, So 1,2,3 will be the month numbers. If \"period\" is selected as 'year', then its the year numbers.\n- **Mileage**: is the number of kms/miles (depending on your preferred length unit) the car has driven in that period.\n- **Energy Cost**: is the cost spent for electricity in that particular period.\n- **Cost per km or mi**  is *energy cost* / *Mileage*\n- **Cumulative Mileage** is the cumulative mileage for that particular period.\n- **Cumulative Cost** is the cumulative cost for electricity for that particular period.\n- **Depreciation per km or mi** is the depreciation by mileage explained at the beginning.\n- **Depreciation per age** is the depreciation by time explained at the beginning.\n- **Cumulative Savings** is running cost savings for driving an electric car when compared to a fossil fuel car, based on the value enter in the *Fuel price* textbox.\n- **Depreciated Car Value** is the estimated actual price based on the depreciation per age and mileage.  \n- **Depreciated Car Value + Savings** is simply adding *Depreciated Car Value* + *Cumulative Savings*. So the expectation is like when one can get the Break-Even for the money we put into buying the car by driving at a cheaper electricity cost when compared to driving a fossil fuel car.\n": "# 购车回本追踪\n\n这个仪表板用来展示车辆随时间推移的折旧价值，以及它的使用历程。\n\n按里程计算车辆折旧有多种方法，常见的是使用每英里折旧率，或者根据数据建立折旧曲线。而因车龄造成的折旧会受品牌、车型、车况和市场需求等多种因素影响。\n\n一般估计，新车在第一年会损失约 15% 到 20% 的价值，之后折旧速度会逐渐放缓。前几年的年折旧率大致如下：\n\n- 第一年：约 15% 到 20%。\n- 第二年：约 10% 到 15%。\n- 第三年及以后：每年约 5% 到 10%。\n\n请注意，这些数值只是估算，实际情况因人而异，有些车型也会比其他车型更保值。\n\n此外，一些研究和专家认为，车辆每行驶 1 英里会损失一定的价值。这里使用的标准损耗率为每英里或每公里 0.20（以你使用的货币计，单位取决于你偏好的长度单位）。\n\n## 文本框中各项数值说明\n\n本面板同时提供两种估算：**按里程折旧** 和 **按车龄折旧**\n\n所以首先需要填写：\n\n- 估算周期（按年或按月）\n- 购车价格\n- 折旧百分比（首年 %），如上所述默认为 20%\n- 每英里或每公里损耗率，如上所述默认为 0.2（以你使用的货币计）\n- 你之前那辆车（或与你的特斯拉同级的燃油车）每英里或每公里的油费\n\n  要计算车辆每英里/每公里的油费，先要知道它每 100 英里/公里消耗多少升油，然后用油耗除以里程。\n\n  例如：某辆车每 100 公里油耗 6 升，油价为每升 1.8€，那么实际油耗为：6/100 = 0.06 L/km\n\n  然后用实际油耗乘以每升油价（以你使用的货币计）就能得到每公里费用。例如 0.06L/km × 1.8€/L = 0.108€/km（按英里或公里计）。\n\n  因此，这辆车每公里的油费约为 0.108€，这就是\"燃油价格\"文本框中应填写的数值。\n\n## 表格中的数据说明\n\n- **周期**：根据下拉列表的选择，可以是\"月\"或\"年\"。选择\"月\"时，从 TeslaMate 开始记录数据的第 1 个月起累计，1、2、3 表示第几个月；选择\"年\"时则表示第几年。\n- **里程**：该周期内车辆行驶的公里数/英里数（取决于你偏好的长度单位）。\n- **电费**：该周期内花费的电费。\n- **每公里或每英里费用**：*电费* / *里程*\n- **累计里程**：截至该周期的累计里程。\n- **累计电费**：截至该周期的累计电费。\n- **每公里或每英里折旧**：即开头介绍的按里程折旧。\n- **车龄折旧**：即开头介绍的按时间折旧。\n- **累计节省**：根据\"燃油价格\"文本框中填写的数值，与燃油车相比开电动车累计节省的使用成本。\n- **折旧后车辆价值**：根据车龄和里程折旧估算出的当前价值。\n- **折旧后车辆价值 + 节省**：即 *折旧后车辆价值* + *累计节省*。可以借此估算，与开燃油车相比，靠更便宜的电费，什么时候能把购车花的钱\"赚\"回来。\n",
